  "starterCode": "import torch, math\n\ndef cv_vit_attention_block(x: list, W_qkv: list, W_out: list, num_heads: int = 2) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **ViT Multi-Head Self-Attention** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, math\n\ndef cv_vit_attention_block(x: list, W_qkv: list, W_out: list, num_heads: int = 2) -> list:\n    t_x, t_qkv, t_out = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(W_qkv, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(W_out, dtype=torch.float32)\n    N, D = t_x.shape\n    d_k = D // num_heads\n    q, k, v = torch.chunk(torch.matmul(t_x, t_qkv), 3, dim=-1)\n    q = q.view(N, num_heads, d_k).transpose(0, 1)\n    k = k.view(N, num_heads, d_k).transpose(0, 1)\n    v = v.view(N, num_heads, d_k).transpose(0, 1)\n    attn = torch.softmax(torch.matmul(q, k.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(d_k), dim=-1)\n    ctx = torch.matmul(attn, v).transpose(0, 1).contiguous().view(N, D)\n    return torch.round(torch.matmul(ctx, t_out), decimals=4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
